<title>ITALY: Italy promises &quot;Euro-tax&quot; will be one-off.</title>
<headline>Italy promises &quot;Euro-tax&quot; will be one-off.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Finance Minister Vicenzo Visco said on Sunday that a planned &quot;Euro-tax&quot; that forms part of the 1997 budget package would remain a one-off levy.</p>
<p>&quot;It will not become structural, it will be paid during 1997 and physically it will be separate from other taxes,&quot; Visco told state television in an interview.</p>
<p>He said details of the charge had not yet been worked out but he anticipated the cost to be up to a maximum of two million lire depending on income levels.</p>
<p>The government intends to raise 13 trillion lire via the tax. The budget package, unveiled on Friday, intends to cut 62.5 trillion lire off next year's deficit.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
